! fp_internal_operand.strap -- AN FP OPERAND IN AN INTERNAL REGISTER
! ($R) WAITS FOR THE E-BOX AND THEN TAKES THE STORE PATH.  Built
! 2026-11-17 with StretchCore's headReady (intWait) and StretchTiming's
! fpInternalOperandClocks (docs/atlas_oracle.md, "Closing the residuals"
! item 8).
!
! THE SOURCE.  Perf. Char. Vol. 1 printed p.3-20 (PDF 38): "The I-box,
! upon decoding an instruction whose fetch operand is an internal
! register, uses the LAAR to store the internal operand address. This is
! because the needed operand is not available during the decoding stage,
! and the mechanism for internal operand fetch already exists for the
! handling of store instructions."  "(By an internal operand address is
! meant address 3, or an address between 5 and 12 inclusive.)"  The
! atlas prints L from $R at 10 clocks a copy and from memory, forwarded,
! at 8 (PDF 95).
!
! THE BODY.  $R gets the FP one by a one-word TI (a load clears $R), as
! the atlas's generator sets it; then eight L(U) from $R, then eight from
! memory (the external control inside the deck: the wait does not apply
! to them).  RES gets the one.
!
! MEASURED, 2026-11-17 (CYCLES in run_tests.sh's run line).  The single
! injections below were run before the M+ index-store and instruction-
! store changes of the same day; both leave this deck's CYCLES where it
! was (re-measured on the final tree), and with the whole preparation
! floor removed (`ib` and the "- 1" together) prep_floor runs in 399,
! fp_internal_operand in 205.
!   the model as of this deck .......................... 208
!   OBSERVED INJECTION, reverted from a saved copy checked with cmp:
!   - intWait forced False (the operand free as soon as the level
!     before it is removed) ............................... FAIL cycles 181
!   Nothing else failed (PC and RES pass).  208 - 181 = 27 over eight
!   copies: the wait is 7 clocks a copy, partly hidden behind the 4-clock
!   decode of the next L.
! The control is decks/prep_floor.strap, which has no internal operand
! and whose CYCLES (349) did not move under this injection.
! prep_floor's injections, run on this deck too: rl_au_remove without
! `ibusy <= ib` and fpIboxCheckClocks = 0 leave it at 208 (it is E-box
! and wait bound, and it has no $X operand); rl_prepare's load without
! the "- 1" gives 205, three clocks FASTER -- observed, not explained
! here; the later decode shifts when the internal level reaches the
! head relative to the E-box.
! RE-PINNED 208 -> 204, 2026-11-17, by an FP look-ahead level's fetch
! yielding the bus to a waiting 1Y/2Y fetch (StretchStorage memCtl,
! R23-9732 Fig. 3.1.21; decks/ibox_supply.strap).  MEASURED with the
! yield removed (fpYields forced False): 208 again, nothing else fails.
! The eight memory L's instruction words now arrive sooner.

        SLC, (8)2000.0

START   L(U), FONE
        TI, 1, FONE, 9.0           ! $R = the FP one
        L(U), $R
        L(U), $R
        L(U), $R
        L(U), $R
        L(U), $R
        L(U), $R
        L(U), $R
        L(U), $R
        L(U), FONE
        L(U), FONE
        L(U), FONE
        L(U), FONE
        L(U), FONE
        L(U), FONE
        L(U), FONE
        L(U), FONE
        ST(U), RES

PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, (8)2200.0

FONE    DD(BU,64,8), (16)0028000000000000
RES     DD(BU,64,8), 0

        END, START
